4000,"stop":1794185878760,"duration":494760}},{"uid":"e19eaee520b01fd1","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/11/#testresult/e19eaee520b01fd1","status":"passed","time":{"start":1794088953000,"stop":1794089428000,"duration":475000}},{"uid":"6c37197e2b6770af","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/10/#testresult/6c37197e2b6770af","status":"passed","time":{"start":1794002955000,"stop":1794003780620,"duration":825620}},{"uid":"b0078cdec0900b1d","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/9/#testresult/b0078cdec0900b1d","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793924518000,"stop":1793924977340,"duration":459340}},{"uid":"b131729cf909a9d7","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/8/#testresult/b131729cf909a9d7","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793830098000,"stop":1793831028270,"duration":930270}},{"uid":"65b1a9c8654127eb","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/7/#testresult/65b1a9c8654127eb","status":"failed","statusDetails":"failed to get device \"edge-dev\" ECDH certificate: unexpected status from GET https://127.0.0.1:443/admin/device/cf1480c4-0ecb-4ec9-8d46-e2484b01b82a/certs: 400\n\nClaude's conclusion:\nOnly this one test ran in this suite so far — no other failure in this run to share a root cause with. I have enough evidence to conclude.\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe test failed in setup, before fault injection was even armed: `evetest/setup.go`'s `onboardEVEDevice` polls Adam's admin `/certs` endpoint for the device's ECDH certificate and gives up after 11 failed attempts (~55s). Live evidence shows the device (`edge-dev`, first boot at `00:48:17`) is unusually slow this run — `top`/`vmstat` on the live device show 35‑49% iowait with 2‑3 processes blocked on I/O and a load average of ~5.5 on a 4-vCPU guest, 5 minutes after boot. The device's `tpmmgr`-generated `EdgeNodeCert` files only land on disk at `00:49:xx`, and the device doesn't actually POST its certs to Adam (`/api/v2/edgedevice/certs`) until `00:50:21` — well past the harness's ~55s polling window, which is why Adam's `deviceCertsGet` kept failing with \"no such file\" and the admin API call eventually returned 400. Device log delivery itself stalled at `00:48:14` and never resumed, consistent with system‑wide I/O starvation delaying boot-critical work rather than a pillar logic bug.\n\nThis is not the same issue as the one prior `TestInfoRetriedAfterServerError` ledger entry (2026‑11‑01), which failed on an unrelated SDN-tunnel `no route to host` flake before the device ever onboarded — tonight's device onboarded and got a network fine, it was just too slow publishing its cert. So this is a **new failure mode** for this test, though it fits the broader recurring theme already in the ledger (e.g. `TestMgmtProxy`, `TestTieBreakerCluster` entries) of Proxmox-host resource contention causing slow disk/CPU on EVE guests on overloaded nights. No other test failed earlier in this run to share a root cause with, and no PR diff was supplied to assess relatedness.","time":{"start":1793753030000,"stop":1793753579740,"duration":549740}},{"uid":"416b98e83188366b","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/6/#testresult/416b98e83188366b","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793659432000,"stop":1793659853220,"duration":421220}}]},"tags":[]},"source":"f14a5dc7a66b354e.json","parameterValues":[]}